---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy — Vraj Patel"
  description="How vrajmpatel.com uses optional PostHog analytics and session replay, and how to change those choices."
>
  <header class="max-w-3xl pb-10 sm:pb-14">
    <p class="font-mono text-xs text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">Site</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.035em] text-slate-950 dark:text-white sm:text-5xl">
      Privacy
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-8 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
      This personal portfolio is a static site. Optional measurement runs only
      after you opt in, and never when your browser asks not to be tracked.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="max-w-3xl space-y-12 text-base leading-8 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 sm:text-lg">
    <section aria-labelledby="choices-heading">
      <h2 id="choices-heading" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-slate-950 dark:text-white">
        Your choices
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-5">
        Analytics and session replay are independent grants. Both default to
        off. Nothing is sent to PostHog until you save a choice that turns a
        grant on. You can change or withdraw those choices from
        <strong class="font-medium text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200">Privacy choices</strong>
        in the footer, or from the banner the first time you visit.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-5">
        If your browser sends a Do Not Track or Global Privacy Control signal,
        this site treats that as a full opt-out. The tracker does not load, and
        a later opt-in on this device is ignored while that signal remains.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="analytics-heading">
      <h2 id="analytics-heading" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-slate-950 dark:text-white">
        Analytics
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-5">
        If you allow analytics, PostHog records page views, page leaves (used
        for bounce rate and session duration), autocaptured clicks and form
        interactions, heatmaps, and web vitals. Person profiles stay
        <code class="font-mono text-sm">identified_only</code>: this site does
        not call <code class="font-mono text-sm">identify()</code> or attach a
        name or account to you.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-5">
        Referrer and UTM source fields may be kept so I can see how people find
        the site. Query strings and URL fragments are stripped from the current
        page URL. Ad click identifiers such as <code class="font-mono text-sm">gclid</code>
        and <code class="font-mono text-sm">fbclid</code> are dropped.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="replay-heading">
      <h2 id="replay-heading" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-slate-950 dark:text-white">
        Session replay
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-5">
        If you allow session replay, PostHog records a masked replay of the
        visit. All inputs are masked, including email, password, and textarea
        fields. Replay can be on while analytics is off, and the reverse.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="storage-heading">
      <h2 id="storage-heading" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-slate-950 dark:text-white">
        What is stored on this device
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-5">
        Your analytics and replay choices are saved in local storage under
        <code class="font-mono text-sm">vrajmpatel-analytics-consent</code>.
        After a grant, PostHog may also set its own first-party cookies or
        local storage keys so page leaves and sessions work. Theme preference
        is stored separately and is not sent to PostHog.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="processor-heading">
      <h2 id="processor-heading" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-slate-950 dark:text-white">
        Who processes the data
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-5">
        Consented events are processed by PostHog on US Cloud. The public
        project token is a browser key, not a personal API key. The site is
        hosted on GitHub Pages. Ingestion currently goes to PostHog’s US
        endpoint unless a first-party proxy host is configured.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="contact-heading">
      <h2 id="contact-heading" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-slate-950 dark:text-white">
        Questions
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-5">
        For a suspected privacy or security problem with this site, use
        <a
          href="https://github.com/basechildren/vrajmpatel.com/security/advisories/new"
          class="underline decoration-slate-300 underline-offset-4 hover:text-blue-700 focus-visible:rounded-sm focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-blue-600 dark:decoration-slate-700 dark:hover:text-blue-400"
        >
          GitHub private vulnerability reporting
        </a>.
        For other questions, use the
        <a
          href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/vrajmp/"
          class="underline decoration-slate-300 underline-offset-4 hover:text-blue-700 focus-visible:rounded-sm focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-blue-600 dark:decoration-slate-700 dark:hover:text-blue-400"
        >
          LinkedIn profile
        </a>
        linked in the footer. This page is a privacy policy for the portfolio,
        not a terms of service.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
